+
+Pay at Hotel – Payment Calculation, Settlement & Refund Rules
+1. Commission and Payment Collection
+The mTrip commission is borne by the merchant and is not an additional charge to the customer.
+For Pay at Hotel bookings, mTrip collects the commission, applicable transaction fee and no-show pre-collection (if enabled) through online payment.
+The commission and no-show pre-collection are deducted from the room amount payable at the hotel.
+The transaction fee is charged separately and calculated on the commission amount only.
+Commission already collected online must not be charged again during merchant settlement.
+2. Discount and Payment Calculation
+When both a Long Stay discount and a coupon are applicable, the Long Stay discount must be applied first, followed by the eligible coupon.
+Each discount must retain its respective funding type (merchant-funded, platform-funded or co-funded) and funding ratio at the time of booking.
+Calculation Rules
+Item
+Calculation
+Final Room Amount
+Original Room Amount − Long Stay Discount − Coupon Discount
+Commission
+Final Room Amount × Commission Rate
+Transaction Fee
+Commission × Transaction Fee Rate
+Pay Now
+Commission + Transaction Fee + No-Show Pre-Collection
+Pay at Hotel
+Final Room Amount − Commission − No-Show Pre-Collection
+TotalCustomer Payment
+Final Room Amount + Transaction Fee
+
+
+
+3. No-Show Policy
+If the no-show policy is disabled, no no-show amount is collected upfront.
+If enabled, the configured no-show rate must be between 1% and 30%.
+If the customer checks in, the pre-collected amount is applied towards the room payment and settled with the merchant.
+If the customer fails to show up, the no-show amount is non-refundable and must be settled with the merchant as compensation for holding the reservation.
+The remaining unpaid hotel balance must not be collected for confirmed no-show bookings.
+For customer cancellations within the allowed cancellation period, refund the commission and any no-show pre-collection. The transaction fee is non-refundable. No no-show payment is due to the merchant. 
+The system must retain the no-show policy and rate applicable at the time of booking.
