+6. Cancellation and Refund Rules
+Cancellation eligibility follows the policy recorded at booking (Consumer PRD Module 8, Section 8.9.1). For eligible customer cancellations, refund all online payments except the transaction fee. For late cancellations and no-shows, no refund is issued; mTrip retains the commission and transaction fee, and the merchant receives the no-show pre-collection. If the merchant or mTrip cancels a confirmed booking before check-in, refund the full online payment, including the transaction fee, regardless of the cancellation deadline. No no-show payment is due to the merchant in this case.
+Partial cancellation and partial refund are out of scope for MVP. Each cancellation applies to one complete Booking ID, including bookings within a multi-hotel trip. For Pay at Hotel, the customer selects either mTrip Wallet or an external bank/e-wallet to receive the full eligible refund, regardless of the original payment split. Example: for an online payment of 30,200 MMK (commission 10,000; transaction fee 200; no-show pre-collection 20,000), an eligible customer cancellation returns 30,000 MMK, a merchant or mTrip cancellation returns 30,200 MMK, and a late cancellation or no-show returns 0 MMK. The unpaid hotel balance is not collected. Refer to Module 24 for refund processing and audit requirements.
